; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Harmonograph
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     pendulum, damping, exponential decay, sine, random, art
; SUMMARY:  Imitates a Victorian drawing machine where swinging pendulums move a pen, slowly dying down into a spiral of loops.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A harmonograph has two or more pendulums. One moves the pen left
;   and right, another moves it up and down, and each swing is a
;   little smaller than the last because of friction. When the swing
;   speeds are in a simple ratio, like 2 to 3, and slightly out of
;   tune, the pen draws looping curves that shrink toward the middle.
;   Every run picks a new ratio, tuning and phase, prints them, and
;   draws a new picture.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Run it again for another drawing. To keep one you like,
;   write down the numbers it prints and put them in the last line.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a swing as a sine wave: amplitude x sin(speed x time + phase)
;   * damping: multiplying by a number a bit less than 1, again and
;     again, which is exponential decay (EXP)
;   * adding two pendulums in each direction
;   * a color that slowly fades as time goes on
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set the detune to exactly 0. Why does the picture become simple?
;   * Make the damping bigger (0.004) for a short, open drawing.
;   * Use three pendulums for x instead of two.
; ============================================================

make "ratios [[1 2] [2 3] [3 4] [3 2] [1 3] [2 5] [4 5] [3 5]]

; Position at time t. Two pendulums in x, two in y. f are speeds,
; p are phases, and everything shrinks by exp(-damp x t).
to harmopoint :t :f1 :f2 :p1 :p2 :damp
  localmake "fade exp minus :damp * :t
  localmake "x 170 * (sin :f1 * :t + :p1) + 90 * (sin :f2 * :t)
  localmake "y 170 * (sin :f2 * :t + :p2) + 90 * (sin :f1 * :t + 90)
  output list :x * :fade :y * :fade
end

to harmonograph :f1 :f2 :p1 :p2 :damp
  print (sentence [harmonograph] :f1 :f2 :p1 :p2 :damp)
  penup setpos harmopoint 0 :f1 :f2 :p1 :p2 :damp
  pendown
  for [t 0 2400 0.25] [
    ; fade from deep blue to pink as the swings die down
    localmake "k :t / 2400
    setpencolor (list 40 + 200 * :k 60 + 40 * :k 160 - 20 * :k)
    setpos harmopoint :t :f1 :f2 :p1 :p2 :damp
    if 0 = remainder int :t * 4 80 [wait 1]
  ]
end

; Pick a ratio, detune the second speed a little, choose phases.
to randomharmonograph
  localmake "r pick :ratios
  localmake "f1 5 * (first :r)
  localmake "f2 5 * (last :r) + ((random 21) - 10) / 300
  harmonograph :f1 :f2 random 360 random 360 0.0008 + (random 8) / 10000
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 247 240]
setpensize 1
randomharmonograph
